# built site — generated by pipeline/build_site.py, deployed by CI, never committed
_site/
__pycache__/
.vercel
.env*

# local render tooling — playwright for render_t2 stills; installed on demand,
# never committed (CI ships its own chromium). See render_t2.py.
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json

# Kaggle API token lives in ~/.kaggle, never here
kaggle.json
access_token

# macOS Finder junk — was tracked, and every render session dirtied it,
# which made the "uncommitted changes" render guard cry wolf.
.DS_Store

# Local narrative review page (build_review.py). Not published: it contains the
# unapproved draft scripts, and it dirties the tree the render guard checks.
sapling-narrative.html

# Local shot-board pages (build_shotboard.py) — same reason as the review page
shotboard-*.html

# Local beat index (BEATMAP.html) and the frames it shows. Same reason again: the
# thumbnails are one frame each out of unapproved working clips, and the page
# exists so a beat can be named in chat, not to be published.
BEATMAP.html
.beatmap-thumbs/

# Candidate render media under a node's takes/ — the pick-of-N frames drawn while
# a beat is being dialled in, ~1 MB each and dozens per beat. Media does not go
# into git; only the frame the founder picks does, promoted deliberately. 002b's
# takes/ held 25 MB of untracked candidates and was one `git add -A` from being
# committed (2026-08-06). Extensions, not the directory, so the yaml provenance
# sidecars that sit beside the pixels stay in the tree where they belong.
genomes/*/nodes/*/takes/**/*.png
genomes/*/nodes/*/takes/**/*.jpg
genomes/*/nodes/*/takes/**/*.mp4
genomes/*/nodes/*/takes/**/*.mp3
genomes/*/nodes/*/takes/**/*.wav
# 001's takes/ is the deliberate exception: a committed v1 archive, all 183 files
# tracked. Ignoring never untracks anything, so those are safe either way — this
# keeps NEW files there behaving as they always have rather than vanishing.
!genomes/sapling/nodes/001-capability-inventory/takes/**

# Render media pulled off the farm boxes into review/. Same hazard as takes/ and
# closed the same way (2026-08-07): 41 clips and 3 wavs were sitting untracked,
# one `git add -A` from the tree, and nothing under review/ has ever been tracked
# — verified with git ls-files before writing this. Extensions, not the
# directory, so the .meta.yaml provenance sidecars that arrive beside every clip
# stay visible: a sidecar is the record of what a render WAS, and it must not be
# hidden along with the pixels it describes.
review/**/*.mp4
review/**/*.mov
review/**/*.webm
review/**/*.png
review/**/*.jpg
review/**/*.mp3
review/**/*.wav

# poll_decisions.py's "when did we last look" note. Not the watermark — the
# watermark is pipeline/founder-answers.jsonl, whose comment ids are what stop a
# reply being recorded twice. This file is a convenience, so it is local-only and
# deleting it costs nothing.
pipeline/.decisions-state.json
